    {
      "op": "finish",
      "diagnosis": "The issue was that email addresses were not normalized before being checked for duplicates, leading to different spellings (case and surrounding whitespace) of the same email address being treated as distinct. The fix involved introducing a `normalize_email` function in `normalize.py` and integrating it into `importer.py` and `store.py`. Specifically, `importer.py` now normalizes emails before checking `store.seen` and adds the normalized email to `store.seen`. `store.py` was updated to normalize emails in its `seen` list upon loading and when adding new contacts, ensuring consistency.",
